sequenceDiagram
    participant Main as Main thread (producer)
    participant Q as requestQueue
    participant S as Semaphore (count)
    participant W as Worker thread (consumer)

    Note over W: Startup - worker calls WaitForSingleObject, count is 0, so it sleeps
    Main->>Main: accept() returns new client socket
    Main->>Q: lock queueMutex, push(socket), unlock
    Main->>S: ReleaseSemaphore (count +1)
    S-->>W: wake up (count -1)
    W->>Q: lock queueMutex, front() + pop(), unlock
    W->>W: read, route, respond, closesocket
    W->>S: WaitForSingleObject again (sleep until next request)
